---
layout: base.njk
title: "The family"
description: "The POAP KINGS products that read from Elixir MCP — the clan, Elixir Drop, the clan agent, the Discord bot and the Clash Royale API docs — plus the Clash Royale things we like but have nothing to do with."
permalink: /family/index.html
canonical: /family
navActive: family
---
{#-
  Two groups, two bylines, and no cross-selling between them.

  Ours say how they fit the hub. Theirs say plainly that they are not
  connected to us. Recommending somebody else's work in the same voice
  you use to sell your own is what makes both of them untrustworthy, so
  the byline changes and the "how it fits" line says "no connection".
-#}
<div class="page-head">
  <div>
    <h1 class="hero-title" style="margin-bottom: 6px">The family</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0; max-width: 62ch">
      Elixir MCP is the hub: it records, and everything else pulls what it
      needs with its own credential. None of them reaches into another, and
      none of them holds a Clash Royale key.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

{%- for g in family %}
<section style="margin-top: 34px">
  <div style="display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line)">
    <h2 style="font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0">{{ g.group }}</h2>
    <span class="footnote" style="margin-left: auto">
      {%- if g.theirs -%}
        not ours, and not connected to us &mdash; we just play them
      {%- else -%}
        a POAP KINGS product
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>

  {%- for p in g.projects %}
  <article style="padding: 22px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-row)">
    <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 10px">
      <span class="tag-chip">{{ p.kind }}</span>
      <span class="chip {% if p.state == 'live' %}chip--ok{% else %}chip--warn{% endif %}"><span class="chip__dot"></span>{{ p.state }}</span>
    </div>
    <h3 class="page-title" style="font-size: 26px; margin: 0 0 8px">{{ p.label }}</h3>
    <p class="lede" style="margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 62ch; font-size: 16px">{{ p.lede }}</p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap">
      <section class="panel" style="flex: 1 1 300px">
        <div class="panel__head">What it is</div>
        <div class="panel__body" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px">
          {%- for point in p.points %}
          <span style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-body)">
            <span style="width: 5px; height: 5px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent-bright); flex: 0 0 auto; margin-top: 7px"></span>{{ point }}
          </span>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="panel" style="flex: 1 1 280px">
        <div class="panel__head">{% if p.theirs %}Where it stands{% else %}How it fits{% endif %}</div>
        <div class="panel__body" style="font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink-body)">{{ p.uses }}</div>
        {%- if not p.theirs %}
        <div class="panel__foot">
          Hub-and-spoke: the hub records, each product pulls what it needs with
          its own credential.
        </div>
        {%- endif %}
      </section>
    </div>

    {#- A slot, not an illustration: a described placeholder is honest
        about a screenshot that does not exist yet, where a drawing of a
        product nobody has seen is not. -#}
    <div class="card-slot" style="margin-top: 18px; height: 220px; border-radius: var(--r-panel); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center">
      <span class="footnote">{{ p.shot }}</span>
    </div>
  </article>
  {%- endfor %}
</section>
{%- endfor %}

<p class="footnote" style="margin: 28px 0 0; max-width: 78ch">
  Everything above that is ours reads the same recorded history your own agent
  can read. Start with <a href="/data">the corpus</a>, or
  <a href="/docs/quickstart">connect an agent</a>.
</p>
